# Git commit messages (Generate Commit Message sparkle button)

When generating a git commit message:

- Use Conventional Commits: `type(scope): subject` (types: feat, fix, refactor, chore, docs, test, ci, build, perf, style).
- The subject line (full first line, including `type:` and optional scope) MUST be at most 100 characters. Never exceed 100.
- Prefer 72 characters or fewer; shorten wording instead of listing every file or component name.
- Use imperative mood (e.g. "add", "fix", "refine"), not past tense.
- Output only the commit subject line unless a body is clearly needed; keep bodies brief.

If the subject would exceed 100 characters, rewrite it shorter before responding.
